<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 24.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 24.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Syd Hrbr Casino     1457.14   2.04</p>
<p> 2   Mayne Nickless	 364.06   7.90</p>
<p> 3   Kidston Gold	   270.83   1.30</p>
<p> 4   Mt Edon Gold	   246.15   2.24</p>
<p> 5   Perilya Mines	  204.65   0.88</p>
<p> 6   Ranger Minerals	200.96   4.20</p>
<p> 7   Equatorial Min	 152.78   0.28</p>
<p> 8   Westpac Prop Tr	108.12   1.73</p>
<p> 9   ST.Barbara Mine	 97.18   0.69</p>
<p>10   Consol Paper	    83.82   2.85</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Jardine Fm China	 4.16   0.62</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    4.37   0.98</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv		5.56   1.31</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		    5.70   5.30</p>
<p> 5   OLS Asia Hldgs	   6.43   0.92</p>
<p> 6   Adel Bton Cement	 7.18   1.72</p>
<p> 7   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	  7.33   0.74</p>
<p> 8   Renison Goldflds	 7.34   5.00</p>
<p> 9   FAI Life ltd	     7.55   0.75</p>
<p>10   Telecasters Nqld	 7.91   5.10</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
